Now we work backwards:
\begin{align*} 1 &= 25 - 1 \cdot 23 \\ &= 24 - 1 \cdot (1199 - 49 \cdot 24) \\ &= 24 - 1199 + 49 \cdot 24 \\ &= 50 \cdot 24 - 1199 \end{align*}
From the above, we see that the inverse of $24$ modulo $1199$ is $50$. Therefore, we multiply both sides of the congruence $24x \equiv 15 \pmod{1199}$ by $50$:
\begin{align*}
24x \cdot 50 &\equiv 15 \cdot 50 \pmod{1199} \\
x &\equiv 750 \pmod{1199}
\end{align*}
We need to find the largest negative integer congruent to $750$ modulo $1199$. This integer can be written as $750 - 1199k$ for some integer $k$. To find the largest negative integer, we need $750 - 1199k < 0$:
\begin{align*}
750 - 1199k &< 0 \\
750 &< 1199k \\
k &> \frac{750}{1199} \approx 0.625
\end{align*}
The smallest integer greater than $0.625$ is $1$. Therefore, we set $k = 1$:
\begin{align*}
x &= 750 - 1199 \cdot 1 \\
x &= 750 - 1199 \\
x &= -449
\end{align*}
Thus, the largest negative integer $x$ satisfying $24x \equiv 15 \pmod{1199}$ is $\boxed{-449}$.

