We need to verify that $n = 32$ satisfies all the original conditions:
\begin{align*}
n &= 32 \quad (\text{divisible by 8}), \\
n-1 &= 31 \quad (\text{divisible by 9}), \\
n-2 &= 30 \quad (\text{divisible by 10}).
\end{align*}

